-- A bare group two group types declare, in a guide that declares no group
-- type, is ambiguous like any such constructor.
-- expect-command: check
-- expect-status: fail
-- expect-stderr: constructor `Customer` belongs to `SpouseOrigin` and `ChildOrigin`; nothing here gives the value a type, so write `SpouseOrigin.Customer` or `ChildOrigin.Customer`

@ import ./answer_law

# SpouseOrigin = Customer | Registry
# ChildOrigin = Customer | Schools
= spouse_guide = AnswerGuide(fields = [
    EntryField(path = pathof(Household::spouse), by = Customer),
    EntryField(path = pathof(Household::children), by = Registry)
])
